{"agent":"Monster3-ADP-fs-7267fe","data":{"by":"Monster3-ADP-fs-7267fe","evidence":{"chunk_findings":[{"chunk":4,"detail":"This new baseline file adds `ignore_imports = [\"ddflow.infra.paths -> shutil\"]` to the `fsio-home` contract. The manifest lists only new/modified baseline files and no removal of any previous entry, so this part grows the fsio-home ignore list (and the other six files in this part do the same). That contradicts the stated CONFORMANCE requirement that baseline ignore lists only shrink. A concrete consequence: `tests/test_architecture_import_contracts.py` will now suppress the direct `shutil` import in `ddflow.infra.paths`, locking in a violation instead of reducing the baseline.","digest":"ad1677535826cb18","location":"tests/guard_baselines/importlinter-fsio-home/ddflow.infra.paths.toml:5","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"tests/guard_baselines/importlinter-fsio-home/ddflow.infra.paths.toml:5"},{"chunk":4,"detail":"The debt comment says the future sweep should move this site behind `ddflow.infra.fsio`, but the operator decision in the context and [r-adapters] require the adapter home to be `ddflow/adapters/` (the new port is `ddflow/adapters/fs.py`). Following this comment would direct the migration to the wrong home and continue keeping filesystem behavior in `ddflow.infra`, contrary to the adapter-port decision.","digest":"0ce7d74e5f0ea5d4","location":"tests/guard_baselines/importlinter-fsio-home/ddflow.infra.paths.toml:3","severity":"LOW","title":"tests/guard_baselines/importlinter-fsio-home/ddflow.infra.paths.toml:3"},{"chunk":5,"detail":"Each new baseline file’s `debt:` comment directs future work to move the site “behind ddflow.infra.fsio / the Fs port,” and the files are placed under the `importlinter-fsio-home/` contract directory. This contradicts the operator decision recorded in the context as [D-adapters-answers]: “the home is ddflow/adapters/ (not ddflow/infra).” Following these baseline comments/contract location sends the shutil strangler into the deprecated `ddflow.infra.fsio` home rather than the new `ddflow.adapters.fs` Fs port, so the change cements the wrong adapter home for the affected `ddflow.services.*` modules.","digest":"73fdda2407571dd5","location":"tests/guard_baselines/importlinter-fsio-home/ddflow.services.cleanup.actions.toml:3 (and the other six new baseline files in this part)","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"tests/guard_baselines/importlinter-fsio-home/ddflow.services.cleanup.actions.toml:3 (and the other six new baseline files in this part)"},{"chunk":7,"detail":"These new debt comments instruct the AU-fs-sweep to move direct `shutil` imports “behind ddflow.infra.fsio / the Fs port,” but [D-adapters-answers] says the home is `ddflow/adapters/` (not `ddflow/infra`). A future sweep that follows this comment will move these call sites to `ddflow.infra.fsio` instead of the approved `ddflow.adapters.fs` port, leaving the site outside the adapter home and perpetuating the architecture violation the contract is meant to ratchet shut.","digest":"712fe9d90281b748","location":"tests/guard_baselines/importlinter-fsio-home/ddflow.services.roborev_branch.toml:3 (also line 3 in ddflow.services.swarm.lanehooks.toml, ddflow.services.upgrade_dryrun._drive.toml, ddflow.services.upgrade_dryrun._steps.toml)","severity":"LOW","title":"tests/guard_baselines/importlinter-fsio-home/ddflow.services.roborev_branch.toml:3 (also line 3 in ddflow.services.swarm.lanehooks.toml, ddflow.services.upgrade_dryrun._drive.toml, ddflow.services.upgrade_dryrun._steps.toml)"},{"chunk":6,"detail":"The debt comment says “AU-fs-sweep moves this site behind ddflow.infra.fsio / the Fs port.” The operator decision [D-adapters-answers] in the intent states the home is `ddflow/adapters/` (not `ddflow/infra`). A future migration following this comment would target `ddflow.infra.fsio`, the wrong home, and leave the dependency outside the required `ddflow.adapters` port; the correct migration target is `ddflow.adapters.fs.Fs`.","digest":"7ff45308d06356a3","location":"tests/guard_baselines/importlinter-fsio-home/ddflow.services.gates.regression_testfix.toml:3 (same comment in the other six files in this part)","severity":"LOW","title":"tests/guard_baselines/importlinter-fsio-home/ddflow.services.gates.regression_testfix.toml:3 (same comment in the other six files in this part)"},{"chunk":1,"detail":"`is_dir` cannot see root or current-directory roots because it only checks `d in self.dirs` or `f.startswith(d + \"/\")`. For `.` this never matches keys such as `a.txt`; for `/` it tests the prefix `//` and never matches `/a.txt`. Input: `FakeFs({\"a.txt\": b\"x\"}).copy_tree(\".\", \"dst\")` raises `FileNotFoundError`, and `FakeFs({\"/a.txt\": b\"x\"}).copy_tree(\"/\", \"/dst\")` raises `FileNotFoundError`; real `shutil.copytree` would copy the contents.","digest":"bebcc63af4313909","location":"ddflow/adapters/fakes/fs.py:is_dir","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"ddflow/adapters/fakes/fs.py:is_dir"},{"chunk":1,"detail":"`move` does not implement the real `shutil.move` rule that an existing directory destination means “put the source inside that directory”. Input: `fs = FakeFs({\"src.txt\": b\"x\"}); fs.mkdir(\"dst\"); fs.move(\"src.txt\", \"dst\")` ends with `fs.files == {\"dst\": b\"x\"}`, making `dst` a file instead of `dst/src.txt`. A directory source into an existing directory likewise merges contents into `dst` rather than creating `dst/<name>`.","digest":"12815fdc4dd6d28d","location":"ddflow/adapters/fakes/fs.py:move","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"ddflow/adapters/fakes/fs.py:move"},{"chunk":1,"detail":"`copy_tree` fails to reject an existing file destination. Input: `fs = FakeFs({\"dst\": b\"x\", \"src/a.txt\": b\"y\"}); fs.mkdir(\"src\"); fs.copy_tree(\"src\", \"dst\")` does not raise `FileExistsError`; it adds `dst/a.txt` while leaving `dst` as a file, producing an impossible state. Real `shutil.copytree` rejects an existing non-directory destination even with `dirs_exist_ok=True`.","digest":"3c943b599fb3f86e","location":"ddflow/adapters/fakes/fs.py:copy_tree","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"ddflow/adapters/fakes/fs.py:copy_tree"},{"chunk":8,"detail":"The whole-change manifest adds 27 new files under `tests/guard_baselines/importlinter-fsio-home/` (for example `ddflow.api.chore.toml`). These are new importlinter baseline ignore entries, so the baseline ignore list grows. This violates the stated CONFORMANCE contract “baseline ignore lists only shrink” [D-unify strangler with ratchets]. With these additions, the guard keeps tolerating direct `ddflow.infra.fsio` imports in the non-home modules instead of shrinking that debt.","digest":"8358b8e6a144b3f3","location":"tests/guard_baselines/importlinter-fsio-home/ddflow.api.chore.toml:1","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"tests/guard_baselines/importlinter-fsio-home/ddflow.api.chore.toml:1"}],"diff_stat":{"deletions":0,"files":0,"insertions":0,"untracked":0},"output_digest":"f9f2352d11e5a8d6","output_file":".ddflow/local/reviews/ADP-fs.rubber_duck.lan-deepseek-v4-pro.20261104T184201Z-4f1dd31b.jsonl","review_kind":"delta","reviewed":[1,3,4,5,6,7,8],"status":"PARTIAL","terminated_by":"SIGTERM","tree_sha":"0346cc3a3905+clean"},"gate":"rubber_duck","reason":"the review was terminated by SIGTERM mid-round after 7 chunk(s) were reviewed (1, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7, 8); those findings are checkpointed, the remaining chunks were not reviewed, which is not a pass"},"id":"ed7ca00b7884f7bdb83d5b89c","kind":"gate.partial","lamport":136161,"schema":1,"subject":"ADP-fs","ts":"2026-11-04T18:51:21.483121Z"}
